 "check": {
  "describe": "Black space with faint twinkling stars; a glowing yellow Sun in the middle, eight thin blue-grey orbit ellipses, Earth's orbit in light blue, small lit planets (Saturn with its ring), 'Earth' labelled with a pulsing ring; 'Solar System' and 'Year 2026.8' at the top; a dark panel below with Earth's facts, eight planet chips (Earth selected) and four speed chips (Week/s selected). Later the planets have moved round their orbits; a drag changes the tilt; tapping Saturn moves the highlight and the label; Year/s makes the year count up fast. Light: the same chart on warm paper with grey star dots, darker orbit lines and a white panel. Mono: black (or white) page, the Sun as a wireframe globe, planets and Saturn's ring as solid onSurface discs, grey orbit lines, the chosen orbit and planet ring in onSurface, outlined chips (the chosen one heavier), no speed control; the year is today's.",
